language variant
language en-zen
name zen
gender male 40

// ZEN — the calm one.
//
// The ACCENT is not in this file: it is voices/en-zen, because espeak-ng
// silently ignores `replace` inside a !v/ variant and only a full voice file may
// redefine a phoneme. What is here is the body — and the body's whole job is to
// be unhurried without being sleepy.

// A NARROW BAND, LOW IN IT. Mid-low and almost level. Calm is not depth and it is
// not slowness; it is the ABSENCE OF URGENCY, and urgency in a voice is pitch
// movement. A range of 26 is enough to sound alive and far too little to sound
// hurried.
pitch 104 130

// Warm, and deliberately short of brilliance. The peak sits at 900 Hz — low
// enough to feel like chest rather than mouth — and everything above 2.5 kHz is
// gently reduced. Sibilance is what makes a voice feel tense, so there is very
// little of it here. The 1.8 kHz point is kept up because that is intelligibility
// and calm is no excuse for mumbling.
tone 260 190 900 235 1800 175 2500 120 3600 70

// An open, relaxed tract: F1 and F2 are broad rather than peaked, which is what
// an unconstricted throat measures like. Nothing above F5 is doing much work.
formant 0 100 124 128
formant 1 104 122 126
formant 2 106 116 118
formant 3 104 108 104
formant 4 100 100  86
formant 5  94  92  66
formant 6  86  84  44
formant 7  80  78  30
formant 8  76  74  22

// BREATH IS THE CALM. An unpressed fold with air moving past it is the sound of
// someone who is not straining, and there is no faster way to tell a listener
// that nothing is wrong. voicing is deliberately below the commanding voices
// (leader 96, overlord 94) — this voice is not holding anything.
breath  2 3 4 4 4 4 3 2
breathw 110 145 160 160 160 160 145 115
voicing 68
roughness 0
flutter 1

// Consonants softened. Every other voice in this cast pushes them up for
// authority; this one lets them settle, because hard consonants read as
// insistence. It stays well clear of mumbling — the tone curve holds 1.8 kHz up
// for exactly that reason.
consonants 70 62

// A large, soft, quiet space. Long enough to suggest a room with air in it,
// quiet enough that it never becomes a hall you are being addressed across.
echo 130 8

// NOTHING INSISTS.
// intonation 1 keeps the full natural melody — this voice is not withholding, it
// is simply not pushing. Stress arrives as a small pitch movement rather than as
// loudness, which is the gentler of the two and the one that does not startle.
intonation 1
stressAmp   14 14 15 15 16 16 17 18
stressAdd    0  4 10 16 22 28 36  44
